<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34587" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pĕpărēthus</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-os</span></b> , i, f.,
		= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πεπάρηθος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>Peparethus</i> (now <i>Piperi</i>), <i>a small island in the
				Ægean Sea</i>, <i>one of the
			Cyclades</i>, <i>famous for wine and oil</i>, <i>with a town of the same name</i>, now <i>Scopelo</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ferax Peparethos olivae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					7, 470</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Liv. 28, 5, 10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">31, 28,
			6</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pĕpărēthĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of</i>
			or <i>belonging to Peparethos</i>, <i>Peparethian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vinum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					14, 7, 9, § 76</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
